<!--m2s--><div class="sn"><p class="sn-h"><span>🔤 What the symbols mean</span><button type="button" class="sn-all" data-sym="*">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class="sn-l"><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="var"><i>g</i></button><span class="sn-r">Say: “g”</span><span class="sn-m">short for the slope (the gradient)</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="prime">□′</button><span class="sn-r">Say: “prime”</span><span class="sn-m">The little mark means “derivative”: how fast the function is changing at this point, like how steep a slope is.</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="sum">Σ</button><span class="sn-r">Say: “sigma” (sum)</span><span class="sn-m">“Add up a whole list.” Below: where to start; above: where to stop. With only a letter below, add over every possible value of it.</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="var"><i>i</i></button><span class="sn-r">Say: “i”</span><span class="sn-m">a label: which knob</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="frac">▭⁄▭</button><span class="sn-r">Say: “over” (the fraction bar)</span><span class="sn-m">The top is divided by the bottom. ½ is 1 divided by 2, which is one half.</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="partial">∂</button><span class="sn-r">Say: “partial” (or “del”)</span><span class="sn-m">The partial-derivative sign: keep every other input still, move just one a tiny bit, and see how fast the result changes.</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="sub">□₁</button><span class="sn-r">Say: “sub” (the small lowered mark)</span><span class="sn-m">A small lowered mark is a number or a label that tells apart several things of the same kind: label 1 and label 2 are the 1st one and the 2nd one.</span></li><li><button type="button" class="sn-s" data-sym="var"><i>u</i></button><span class="sn-r">Say: “u”</span><span class="sn-m">a direction: a list of numbers of length 1 that only says which way</span></li></ul><p class="sn-seen"><span>Explained above:</span><button type="button" class="sn-c" data-sym="fx">□( )</button><button type="button" class="sn-c" data-sym="var"><i>L</i></button><button type="button" class="sn-c" data-sym="theta">θ</button><button type="button" class="sn-c" data-sym="mul">□□</button><button type="button" class="sn-c" data-sym="nabla">∇</button><button type="button" class="sn-c" data-sym="cdot">·</button></p></div><!--/m2s--></div><div class="pf-why">Why: Multivariable chain rule: each θᵢ moves at speed uᵢ.</div></li><li><div class="pf-st"><div class="kx kx-w"><div class="kxf"><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>u</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>≥</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi>u</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\nabla L\\cdot u\\ \\ge\\ -\\|\\nabla L\\|\\,\\|u\\|=-\\|\\nabla L\\|</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="katex-base"><span class="katex-strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="katex-base"><span class="katex-strut" style="height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mspace"> </span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≥</span><span class="mspace"> </span><span 